  <notes>
    - Under strategy (b), this task is mostly a no-op for LegalWorkspace (files stayed put). Confirm WorkspaceLayoutWizard's consumer relationship separately.
    - If WorkspaceLayoutWizard doesn't consume the section registry, this task simplifies to LegalWorkspace-only.

    === Completion notes (2026-07-02, task-execute FULL rigor, solo dispatch by Wave 11 parent) ===

    Grep results (from repository worktree):
      • `grep '@spaarke/legal-workspace' src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/` — only appears in JSDoc/comments of src/index.ts + SmartToDoDialog.tsx. NO actual `import ... from '@spaarke/legal-workspace'` in any LegalWorkspace source file. LegalWorkspace's internal code uses relative paths exclusively.
      • `grep '@spaarke/legal-workspace' src/solutions/WorkspaceLayoutWizard/` — ZERO matches.
      • `grep 'sectionRegistry' src/solutions/WorkspaceLayoutWizard/` — ONE match, and it is a comment in ArrangeStep.tsx (line 1202) describing sectionRegistry.ts's runtime console.warn behavior, NOT an import.

    Config inspection:
      • LegalWorkspace tsconfig.json — no `@spaarke/legal-workspace` in `paths`.
      • LegalWorkspace vite.config.ts — no `@spaarke/legal-workspace` in `resolve.alias` or `sharedLibPaths` or react `include`.
      • WorkspaceLayoutWizard tsconfig.json — paths only cover `@spaarke/auth` + `@spaarke/ui-components`.
      • WorkspaceLayoutWizard vite.config.ts — minimal config; only `@` alias to `./src`.

    Decisions:
      1. **LegalWorkspace**: NO CHANGE required. Under RE-EXPORT strategy (b), files stay physically at `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/src/` and LegalWorkspace continues consuming its own sectionRegistry.ts + registration modules via relative paths (unchanged behavior). Adding a file: dep for `@spaarke/legal-workspace` (POML step 3 lists as OPTIONAL) would create a self-referential dep (LegalWorkspace → Spaarke.LegalWorkspace/src/index.ts → re-exports FROM LegalWorkspace/src/index.ts) with no consumer needing it. Per CLAUDE.md §11 (Component Justification — cost-of-doing-nothing rule), the self-dep has no concrete failure mode; skip it.
      2. **WorkspaceLayoutWizard**: NO CHANGE required. It does NOT consume the section registry, LegalWorkspaceApp, or any other symbol from `@spaarke/legal-workspace`. Task 022's mirror-pattern (file: dep + Vite sharedLibPaths + tsconfig paths) does not apply.

    Verification (tsc baseline):
      • `npx tsc --noEmit` in `src/solutions/LegalWorkspace/`: pre-existing errors only (missing @types/jest for test files, unused-variable warnings, and unresolved `@spaarke/ai-widgets/*` subpath imports — same baseline as pre-task). No new errors introduced (no changes made).
      • `npx tsc --noEmit` in `src/solutions/WorkspaceLayoutWizard/`: pre-existing errors only (missing @testing-library/react types, existing LayoutJson.scope + IWizardShellProps.title mismatches). No new errors introduced (no changes made).

    Acceptance criteria status:
      • LegalWorkspace builds without changes to functionality — ✅ (no changes)
      • WorkspaceLayoutWizard builds without changes to functionality — ✅ (no changes)
      • Both consumers can import from @spaarke/legal-workspace if they choose to — ⚠️ Partial. LegalWorkspace currently CANNOT (no path/alias), but neither wants to; adding the wiring for a hypothetical future consumer violates §11 cost-of-doing-nothing. WorkspaceLayoutWizard is the same. If a future task legitimately needs one of them to consume the shared package, that task adds the dep at that point.

    Files modified: NONE.

    Deviations from POML:
      • Step 3 (add file: dep to LegalWorkspace/package.json) — deliberately skipped per POML text ("optional for LegalWorkspace-internal code") + CLAUDE.md §11 justification rule. Documented above.
      • Step 5 (npm install + npm run build) — skipped as vacuously satisfied (no package.json / config changes triggering a re-install; tsc-noEmit verified baseline both projects).
      • Step 6 (TASK-INDEX.md update) — per parent dispatch instructions, main session handles TASK-INDEX.md.

    Quality gates (Step 9.5): SKIP (no code files modified — analog to POML documentation-only exemption).
  </notes>

